---
/**
 * Field note: "Should I learn Python, SQL, or R?"
 * → /field-notes/python-sql-or-r/
 *
 * Its own look, and deliberately none of the other three bare notes: an
 * arcade battle screen. Dotted-grid violet night, pixel type for the labels,
 * one saturated color per language, and short blocks throughout. The note
 * argues for picking a main, so the page is built to be read on a phone in
 * under two minutes.
 *
 * Both drawings are original SVG. The type chart is a real table, so it
 * survives a screen reader and reflows on a narrow screen.
 *
 * Inter is already loaded site-wide (ThemeHead.astro); only Silkscreen and
 * Outfit are imported here.
 */
---

<div class="psr">
  <div class="psr-inner">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="psr-hero">
      <p class="psr-kicker">Field note &middot; Careers in data</p>
      <h1>Don&rsquo;t pick one. Main one.</h1>
      <p class="psr-dek">
        &ldquo;Python, SQL, or R?&rdquo; is &ldquo;which Pokemon is the
        best?&rdquo; with a salary attached. Same answer: it depends on what
        you are facing, you carry a team, and you get one favorite.
      </p>

      <!-- ============ DRAWING 1: the cycle ============ -->
      <figure class="psr-fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 272" role="img" aria-labelledby="psr-cycle">
          <title id="psr-cycle"
            >A rock-paper-scissors cycle with three nodes. SQL beats Python at
            pipelines, Python beats R at glue, and R beats SQL at statistics.
            The arrows form a closed loop, so no node wins outright.</title
          >
          <defs>
            <marker
              id="psr-head"
              viewBox="0 0 10 10"
              refX="8"
              refY="5"
              markerWidth="5"
              markerHeight="5"
              orient="auto-start-reverse"
            >
              <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="p-fill-dim" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <!-- arcs, drawn first so the nodes sit on top -->
          <g class="p-arc">
            <path d="M196 74 Q246 96 252 148" marker-end="url(#psr-head)" />
            <path d="M240 226 Q160 258 80 226" marker-end="url(#psr-head)" />
            <path d="M68 148 Q74 96 124 74" marker-end="url(#psr-head)" />
          </g>
          <g class="p-arc-label">
            <text x="268" y="116" text-anchor="middle">pipelines</text>
            <text x="160" y="266" text-anchor="middle">glue</text>
            <text x="52" y="116" text-anchor="middle">stats</text>
          </g>

          <!-- node: SQL / rock -->
          <g>
            <circle cx="160" cy="54" r="42" class="p-node p-sql" />
            <path d="M144 48 l8 -11 15 -3 12 8 -2 12 -14 6 -15 -3 z" class="p-glyph" />
            <text x="160" y="72" text-anchor="middle" class="p-name">SQL</text>
          </g>

          <!-- node: Python / paper -->
          <g>
            <circle cx="256" cy="196" r="42" class="p-node p-py" />
            <path d="M242 178 h22 l10 10 v20 h-32 z" class="p-glyph" />
            <path d="M264 178 v10 h10" class="p-glyph-line" />
            <text x="256" y="220" text-anchor="middle" class="p-name p-name--long">PYTHON</text>
          </g>

          <!-- node: R / scissors -->
          <g>
            <circle cx="64" cy="196" r="42" class="p-node p-r" />
            <path d="M54 172 l18 26 M74 172 l-18 26" class="p-glyph-line" />
            <circle cx="53" cy="203" r="5" class="p-glyph-line" />
            <circle cx="75" cy="203" r="5" class="p-glyph-line" />
            <text x="64" y="224" text-anchor="middle" class="p-name">R</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          Every ranking of these three closes into a loop. No square on the
          chart says &ldquo;always wins.&rdquo;
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 01 ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num">01 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; The question</p>
      <h2>Start with the work you expect to do.</h2>
      <p>
        The useful question is which language you will use regularly enough
        to learn well. Your team&rsquo;s codebase matters as much as a list of
        language features.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 02 ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num psr-num--sql">02 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; SQL</p>
      <h2>SQL is worth learning whichever you choose.</h2>
      <p>
        SQL is central to warehouse analytics: transformations, BI queries,
        and the models behind a semantic layer. Even if you spend most of
        your day in Python or R, you will often need to read and change it.
      </p>
      <p class="psr-note">
        Learning the syntax is only a start. You also need to understand grain,
        avoid joins that duplicate rows, and check whether the source data
        is ready to use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 03 ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num psr-num--py">03 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Python</p>
      <h2>Python covers a lot of the day-to-day work.</h2>
      <p>
        APIs, automation, notebooks, and machine learning give you plenty of
        reasons to choose Python. It is a useful main when your week includes
        several kinds of programming.
      </p>
      <p class="psr-note">
        Check how your team deploys and maintains that work too. The language
        used for a prototype may differ from the one used to serve it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 04 ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num psr-num--r">04 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; R</p>
      <h2>R is a strong choice for statistical work.</h2>
      <p>
        Forecasting, survival analysis, mixed models, experimental design, and
        spatial statistics are good reasons to learn R. If those occupy much
        of your week, it may be the most useful language to know well.
      </p>
      <p class="psr-note">
        Before planning to port an analysis, check how it will be maintained.
        Translating the code also means checking that the results still
        agree.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 05: the type chart ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num">05 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; The type chart</p>
      <h2>Pick by the battle you fight every week.</h2>
      <table class="psr-chart">
        <caption>Effectiveness by job. Three dots means reach for it first.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Job</span></th>
            <th scope="col" class="th-sql">SQL</th>
            <th scope="col" class="th-py">PY</th>
            <th scope="col" class="th-r">R</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Production pipelines</th>
            <td class="c-sql"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">3 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-py"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">2 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-r"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">BI and self-serve</th>
            <td class="c-sql"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">3 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-py"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-r"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Glue and automation</th>
            <td class="c-sql"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-py"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">3 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-r"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">ML in production</th>
            <td class="c-sql"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-py"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">3 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-r"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Forecasting and stats</th>
            <td class="c-sql"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-py"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">2 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-r"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">3 of 3</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Research and prototypes</th>
            <td class="c-sql"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">1 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-py"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">2 of 3</span></td>
            <td class="c-r"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;</span><span class="sr-only">3 of 3</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="psr-note">
        My chart, from my seat. Redraw it for the jobs on your own calendar,
        then read off the column with the most weight.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 06: the party ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num">06 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; The party</p>
      <h2>Three on the belt. One you actually send out first.</h2>

      <figure class="psr-fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 96" role="img" aria-labelledby="psr-belt">
          <title id="psr-belt"
            >Six party slots. Three are filled with SQL, Python, and R, the SQL
            slot carries a star marking it as the main, and three slots are
            still empty.</title
          >
          <!-- filled slots -->
          <g>
            <rect x="7" y="20" width="46" height="46" rx="8" class="p-slot p-slot-sql" />
            <circle cx="30" cy="43" r="13" class="p-orb p-orb-sql" />
            <text x="30" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="p-slot-t">SQL</text>
            <path d="M30 3 l3.2 6.6 7.3 1 -5.3 5.1 1.3 7.2 -6.5 -3.4 -6.5 3.4 1.3 -7.2 -5.3 -5.1 7.3 -1 z" class="p-star" />
          </g>
          <g>
            <rect x="59" y="20" width="46" height="46" rx="8" class="p-slot p-slot-py" />
            <circle cx="82" cy="43" r="13" class="p-orb p-orb-py" />
            <text x="82" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="p-slot-t">PY</text>
          </g>
          <g>
            <rect x="111" y="20" width="46" height="46" rx="8" class="p-slot p-slot-r" />
            <circle cx="134" cy="43" r="13" class="p-orb p-orb-r" />
            <text x="134" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="p-slot-t">R</text>
          </g>
          <!-- empty slots -->
          <rect x="163" y="20" width="46" height="46" rx="8" class="p-slot p-slot-empty" />
          <rect x="215" y="20" width="46" height="46" rx="8" class="p-slot p-slot-empty" />
          <rect x="267" y="20" width="46" height="46" rx="8" class="p-slot p-slot-empty" />
        </svg>
        <figcaption>The empty slots are the point. Something else is coming.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        There is a difference between reading a language, changing existing
        code, writing your own, and maintaining it in production. For
        warehouse analytics, I would aim to maintain SQL and your main
        language confidently, and be able to read and adapt the third.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 07 ============ -->
    <section class="psr-card">
      <p class="psr-num">07 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; What transfers</p>
      <h2>Syntax was always the cheap part, and gen AI made it cheaper.</h2>
      <p>
        Understanding grain, joins, sampling, and what a number means will
        help you in all three. Learn those while working in a language you
        use regularly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CLOSER ============ -->
    <section class="psr-close">
      <p class="psr-num">The rule</p>
      <p class="psr-shout">Main the language your week is made of.</p>
      <p>For analytics work, learn SQL alongside your main. Keep the third
        familiar enough to read and adapt.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ TITLE BLOCK ============ -->
    <footer class="psr-foot">
      <dl class="psr-block">
        <div><dt>Note</dt><dd>Python, SQL, or R</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Field</dt><dd>Careers in data</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Drawn by</dt><dd>Alejandro Berrizbeitia</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Verdict</dt><dd>It depends</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="psr-foot-h">Go deeper</p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://r4ds.hadley.nz/">R for Data Science</a>. The fastest
        route to competent R, free online.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://otexts.com/fpp3/">Forecasting: Principles and Practice</a>.
        Why the forecasting niche stayed in R.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://docs.getdbt.com/">dbt documentation</a>. What
        production-grade SQL looks like once it is a codebase.
      </p>
      <p class="psr-back">
        <a href="/field-notes/">← All field notes</a>
        <a href="/">aleberriz.com</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@600;800&family=Silkscreen:wght@400;700&display=swap');

  /* Arcade battle screen. Scoped, so none of this reaches another note. */
  .psr {
    --void: #0b0716;
    --panel: #150d28;
    --txt: #d8d0ee;
    --dim: #948aba;
    --rule: rgba(182, 255, 61, 0.16);
    --lime: #b6ff3d;
    --sql: #3ad9ff;
    --py: #ffd23f;
    --r: #ff5c8a;

    min-height: 100vh;
    color: var(--txt);
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background-color: var(--void);
    background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(182, 255, 61, 0.11) 1.5px, transparent 1.5px);
    background-size: 22px 22px;
  }

  .psr-inner {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.15rem 3.5rem;
  }

  .psr p { margin: 0 0 0.9rem; }
  .psr a { color: var(--lime); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .psr a:hover { color: var(--sql); }

  .psr-kicker,
  .psr-num,
  .psr-foot-h,
  .psr-back,
  .psr-block dt {
    font-family: Silkscreen, ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .psr-num--sql { color: var(--sql); }
  .psr-num--py { color: var(--py); }
  .psr-num--r { color: var(--r); }

  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  .psr-hero { padding: 3.25rem 0 2.25rem; }
  .psr-hero h1 {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 1rem;
    font-family: Outfit, Inter, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 10vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: #fff;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .psr-dek {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: #b3a8d4;
    max-width: 34ch;
  }

  /* ---------- drawings ---------- */
  .psr-fig { margin: 2rem 0 0; }
  .psr-fig svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 2px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .psr-fig figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .p-node { stroke: #0b0716; stroke-width: 3; }
  .p-sql { fill: var(--sql); }
  .p-py { fill: var(--py); }
  .p-r { fill: var(--r); }
  .p-glyph { fill: #0b0716; }
  .p-glyph-line { fill: none; stroke: #0b0716; stroke-width: 4; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .p-name {
    font-family: Silkscreen, monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: #0b0716;
  }
  .p-name--long { font-size: 10px; }
  .p-arc path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--dim);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }
  .p-fill-dim { fill: #948aba; }
  .p-arc-label text {
    font-family: Silkscreen, monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--lime);
  }

  .p-slot { fill: none; stroke-width: 2.5; }
  .p-slot-sql { stroke: var(--sql); }
  .p-slot-py { stroke: var(--py); }
  .p-slot-r { stroke: var(--r); }
  .p-slot-empty { stroke: #3b3055; stroke-dasharray: 5 5; }
  .p-orb-sql { fill: var(--sql); }
  .p-orb-py { fill: var(--py); }
  .p-orb-r { fill: var(--r); }
  .p-star { fill: var(--lime); }
  .p-slot-t {
    font-family: Silkscreen, monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--dim);
  }

  /* ---------- sections ---------- */
  .psr-card,
  .psr-close {
    padding: 2.25rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .psr-card h2,
  .psr-close h2 {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0.9rem;
    font-family: Outfit, Inter, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 6.4vw, 1.9rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #fff;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .psr-note {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    padding-left: 0.95rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--lime);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    color: #b3a8d4;
  }

  /* ---------- type chart ---------- */
  .psr-chart {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .psr-chart caption {
    caption-side: bottom;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--dim);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .psr-chart th,
  .psr-chart td {
    padding: 0.55rem 0.2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .psr-chart thead th {
    font-family: Silkscreen, monospace;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .th-sql { color: var(--sql); }
  .th-py { color: var(--py); }
  .th-r { color: var(--r); }
  .psr-chart tbody th {
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: left;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .psr-chart td {
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .c-sql { color: var(--sql); }
  .c-py { color: var(--py); }
  .c-r { color: var(--r); }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* ---------- closer ---------- */
  .psr-shout {
    font-family: Outfit, Inter, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 7.6vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--lime);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* ---------- title block ---------- */
  .psr-foot {
    padding: 2rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  .psr-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    background: var(--rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .psr-block > div { padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem; background: var(--panel); }
  .psr-block dt { margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }
  .psr-block dd { margin: 0; color: #fff; }
  .psr-foot-h { margin-bottom: 0.55rem; color: var(--lime); }
  .psr-back { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; padding-top: 0.9rem; }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .psr-block { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .psr-chart { font-size: 0.95rem; }
  }

  /* ---------- present mode ---------- */
  :global(html.present) .psr { font-size: 1.2rem; }
</style>
